  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore High-Performance Buffer Optimization Update\n\n      Architecture and Performance Overhaul\n      - Unified Memory Operations: Eliminated legacy custom FastCopy SIMD loops and pointer pinning overhead. Migrated the entire buffer infrastructure to leverage Net 9 Span CopyTo intrinsics, achieving a cleaner architecture with optimal hardware-level execution.\n      - Optimized Text Transcoding: Refactored character serialization logic by replacing Encoding UTF8 GetByteCount with GetMaxByteCount strategy, eliminating redundant string scanning passes.\n      - Zero Allocation Guarantee: Eradicated minor heap allocation overhead during large-scale resizing, ensuring a pure zero GC profile across all workloads.\n\n      Performance Results\n      - Byte Operations: Methods including Shift, Unshift, Remove, and Resize under heavy memory overlap conditions now execute 2 to 3 times faster. Throughput reaches physical hardware limits at approximately 17 GB per second.\n      - Character Processing: Append and Write operations for char arrays demonstrate a 3 to 4 times speed increase, significantly reducing latency for high-frequency text frames and socket streams.",
